  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A weak system will bring scattered showers tonight.  \n\nA shortwave will move through the Great Lakes tonight with a weak \nsurface low sliding across the region. Scattered showers will \ndevelop tonight along a northward advancing warm front and arrival \nof a strengthening low level jet. A weak cold frontal passage will \nend the shower activity by Wednesday morning. Rainfall amounts will \nbe light, generally a tenth to quarter inch across the western \nSouthern Tier, tapering to just a trace to few hundredths closer to \nLake Ontario.  \n  \nKEY MESSAGE 2...Moderating temperatures through the end of the week.\n\nOmega block developing across the northern half of the country \nthrough the end of the week. We will be on the downstream side of \nthe upper ridge, favoring large-scale subsidence as surface high\npressure builds across the region. This will support a moderating\ntemperature trend through the end of the week. The placement of\na warm frontal boundary will determine how warm some areas get.\nHighest confidence in daytime temperatures reaching the 60s to \nperhaps lower 70s will be across western New York.",
